{%- comment -%}
  The author block at the foot of a blog post.

  A post picks its author with one front matter key:

      author: courtney-hood

  Leave it out and you get whoever authors.json names as the default, which is
  Robert. That is why fifty one existing posts needed no edit at all.

  Everything comes from src/_data/authors.json so a name, a job title or a
  photo is changed in exactly one place, not across fifty posts and three
  templates.

  On the heading: it is a real h2, styled as handwriting, rather than one of the
  .sketch-note divs used elsewhere in this footer. Those are position:absolute
  and display:none below 640px, which is fine for decoration but would delete
  the section's accessible name on every phone. The arrow beside it is the
  decorative half and is aria-hidden, so it can disappear on small screens
  without taking the heading with it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign authorSlug = author | default: authors.default -%}
{%- assign bio = false -%}
{%- for person in authors.people -%}
  {%- if person.slug == authorSlug -%}{%- assign bio = person -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- comment -%}
  An unknown slug falls back to the default rather than rendering an empty
  block, so a typo in front matter degrades to "written by Robert" instead of a
  hole in the page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless bio -%}
  {%- for person in authors.people -%}
    {%- if person.slug == authors.default -%}{%- assign bio = person -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endunless -%}

<aside class="cf-author" aria-labelledby="cf-author-heading">
  <h2 id="cf-author-heading" class="cf-author-label">
    written by
    <svg class="cf-author-arrow" width="44" height="38" viewBox="0 0 44 38" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <path d="M34 4 C33 15, 28 26, 17 32" class="sketch-arrow" />
      <path d="M26 32 L15 34 L21 24" class="sketch-arrow" />
    </svg>
  </h2>

  <div class="cf-author-row">
    <a href="{{ bio.url }}" class="cf-author-avatar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
      <img
        src="{{ bio.photo }}"
        alt=""
        width="420" height="420"
        loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
    </a>

    <div class="cf-author-text">
      <p class="cf-author-name">
        <a href="{{ bio.url }}">{{ bio.name }}</a>
      </p>
      <p class="cf-author-title">{{ bio.title }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</aside>
